		%
		\paragraph{Generalization with remainder variables}

		Our method is currently designed for triangle meshes with a computational cost sublinear to the number of triangles. However, theoretically, this approach is not constrained due to the strong capability of remainder variables in expressing uncertainty and approximation errors. Just like how we handle area light sources, future work could explore extensions to near-specular vertices, non-planar triangles, and triangle aggregations, which could no longer depend on the number of triangles in the scene but rather on the actual geometric complexity.

