        Let $d, D, n$ be positive integers such that $d \leqslant D$.
        Then there exists a nonempty Zariski open subset $U \subset V_{n, d} \times V_{n, D}^{n - 1}$ such that, for every $\bg \in U$, the Newton polytope of the minimal polynomial of $\ideal{\bx' - \bg}^{(\infty)} \cap \KK[x_1^{(\infty)}]$ is the one given by Theorem~\ref{theorem_general_specialized} with $\nu = n$.
    \end{theorem}

