For each terrain, eight Super-Gaussians are used, meaning each terrain is defined by $8 \times 8 = 64$ parameters. Based on experimental results, this dimensionality has been found to be small enough for CMA-MAE to efficiently explore the search space and is sufficient to generate a large diversity of terrains.
